meta {
  name: 40 List Grouped Samples (Grouping Settings)
  type: http
  seq: 40
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/accession/order-samples/grouped?page=1
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

params:query {
  page: 1
  ~status: NEW
  ~collectionStatus: PENDING
  ~search: ACC-00001
  ~tatStatus: WITHIN
  ~dateFrom: 2026-07-01
  ~dateTo: 2026-07-31
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{businessAccessToken}}
}

tests {
  test("200 OK", function () {
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(200);
  });
  test("order-first: each order carries orderId + groups + sampleIds", function () {
    const d = res.getBody().data;
    if (d.length) {
      expect(d[0]).to.have.property("orderId");
      expect(d[0]).to.have.property("groups");
      expect(d[0]).to.have.property("sampleIds");
      if (d[0].groups.length) {
        expect(d[0].groups[0]).to.have.property("barcode");
        expect(d[0].groups[0]).to.have.property("sampleIds");
      }
    }
  });
}

docs {
  Grouped, **order-paginated** in-house list (10 orders/page) — the same filters
  as `01 List Samples`, but **order-first**: the Order ID is ALWAYS the top-level
  grouping and the pagination unit; groups never cross order boundaries. Within
  each order, samples are grouped into final groups by the tenant's **current
  grouping mode** (computed live, not the frozen barcode), so the displayed
  grouping, the shared barcode and the action scope always follow the live Group
  Settings — even after the mode is changed. The in-house-orders page renders +
  scopes actions from this response.

  Grouping mode (`GET/PUT /tenant/accession-settings/grouping-mode`,
  `AccessionGroupingMode`) determines the within-order groups:

  - `SAMPLE_NAME` (Sample-wise) — one final group per sample (each acted on alone).
  - `ORDER` (Order-wise) — one final group for the whole order.
  - `DEPARTMENT` (Department-wise) — one final group per Order + Department.
  - `DEPARTMENT_SAMPLE_NAME` (Department + Sample-wise) — one per
    Order + Department + Sample (default).

  Supports the same filters as `01 List Samples`, including `collectionStatus`
  (`PENDING` | `PARTIAL` | `COLLECTED`) — order-level collection progress derived
  from the order's workflow items' `collectedAt`, independent of the 15-stage
  `status` lifecycle.

  ## Each order (top-level) carries

  - `orderId` + `order` — the order id and its header context (patient, referral).
  - `groupingMode` — the tenant's current mode (FE layout hint).
  - `collectionStatus` — order-level collection progress (`PENDING` | `PARTIAL` |
    `COLLECTED`), powering the §A.6 "Collection Status" column.
  - `sampleIds[]` — all sample ids in the order.
  - `groups[]` — the final (barcode) groups within the order.

  ## Each final group carries

  - `groupKey` — `${orderId}::${modeKey}` (deterministic from the current mode).
  - `barcode` — the group's shared barcode, or null when the members carry
    differing/blank barcodes (e.g. cleared after a mode change → shows
    "No barcode" until a fresh Assign Barcode).
  - `department: { id, name } | null` — the single distinct department, else null.
  - `sampleLabel: string | null` — the single distinct sample name, else null.
  - `samples[]` — the group's list rows (each with `tatStatus` + `departmentName`).
  - `sampleIds[]` — the flat set a group status action targets (sent to a
    `bulk/<action>`); a status change cascades to every sample in the group.

  `meta.total` / `meta.totalPages` count **orders**, not groups or samples.

  **Where did I send it (sender's filters).** `destinationBranchId` (UUID): only samples Sent RIGHT NOW to that
  branch (status Sent + a live INTERNAL transfer to it; a sample the receiving branch sent back, "Sent - Repeated",
  still counts because it stays Sent until the sender decides; one the sender repeated or retrieved does not).
  `externalPartnerName`: only samples Forwarded right now to a partner whose name contains the text (case-insensitive,
  trimmed, max 200). `logisticsType`: now matches the TRANSFER's logistics type of a sample that is Sent / Forwarded /
  Outsourced (a Send, Forward or Outsource records the logistics on the transfer, never on the sample; the sample's
  own column is kept as an alternative for older rows). `outsourceCenterId` and `sendDate` / `forwardDate` /
  `outsourceDate` already filtered on the transfer. All of them also apply to `/summary` (the tab counts) and
  `/grouped`.

  **Send details on every row.** The row's latest transfer (`transfers[0]`) now also carries
  `externalPartnerName`, `sendDate`, `sendTime`, `sampleForm`, `logisticsType`, `logisticsPerson`, `createdAt`,
  `outsourceCenterId` and the resolved names `destinationBranchName` (INTERNAL) and `outsourceCenterName`
  (OUTSOURCE) - resolved in one batched lookup per page, deactivated branches / centers included; a name is absent /
  null when there is nothing to name. The In-House list shows them in its "Send Details" column.
}
